    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\nI implemented the daily-limit rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`:\n\n- Added a check that returns **429 (`HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`)** when 100 or more owners already have today's `registrationDate`, placed right after the new owner's `registrationDate` is defaulted to today.\n- Added a `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` helper that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` matches the given date, mirroring the style of the existing `countOwnersInCity`/`countNamesakes` helpers.\n\nThe acceptance test (`createMany(100)` then expect the 101st to be `429`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
